{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:0.2", "PA_ja_238:0.3"], "en": "The Book of Pairs (Dukanipāta), Chapter on Sandals (Upāhanavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:0.4", "PA_ja_238:1.1"], "en": "8. The Ekapada Jātaka “Come now, dear father,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:1.2"], "en": "[teach me] that single word which is based on many meanings.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:1.3"], "en": "“Tell me something inclusive,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:1.4"], "en": "by which we may accomplish our purpose.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:2.1"], "en": "“The state of being skilled, my dear, is the one word;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:2.2"], "en": "It is expressed through words of manifold meaning;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:2.3", "PA_ja_238:2.4"], "en": "it is conjoined with virtue and brought forth by patience.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:2.5", "PA_ja_238:2.6"], "en": "\"It is enough to bring happiness to friends and suffering to enemies.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_238:3.1"], "en": "Thus ends the Eighth Jātaka, the Ekapada-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
